ric, not willing to further education. Communication difficulty could be mitigated by crew; but for long flights, clear communication is critical. However positive atmosphere suggests good interpersonal relations despite difficulty.\n\nB: strong stress handling, conscientious, technical (weather, computer). Weakness: nasty remarks (crew morale), weak memory for numbers (could be mitigated). No positive teamwork.\n\nD: strong responsibility, problem solving, concentration, adequate response. Weakness: hot temper, know\u2011it\u2011all (crew friction). No positive teamwork.\n\nA: strong anticipatory, leadership, spatial vision (navigation). Weakness: unorganized, show\u2011off, not open to ideas, difficulty taking criticism. No explicit teamwork.\n\nThus C appears best overall despite communication difficulty. The communication difficulty is a notable weakness, but the positive atmosphere may offset. Also C's egocentric attitude could affect teamwork. But overall, C's reliability and calmness are crucial.\n\nThus I will provisionally prefer Candidate C, but note uncertainty about communication difficulty severity. Also note that if other agents have positive teamwork info for A or D, could shift.\n\nNow produce public message."}
